    category: "Guides",
    status: "published",
    updated: "2026-11-08T10:00:00.000Z",
  },
  {
    id: "small",
    title: "The small details are the experience",
    slug: "the-small-details",
    summary: "The quiet decisions that make a product easier to live with.",
    body: "The details work together: a readable label, a useful error, a draft that survives a failed save. Each one builds trust.",
    category: "Stories",
    status: "review",
    updated: "2026-11-07T11:30:00.000Z",
  },
  {
    id: "release",
    title: "A new chapter for the library",
    slug: "a-new-chapter",
    summary: "A look at the foundations behind our next release.",
    body: "We are spending this chapter on the components people use every day. Forms, navigation, content views, and the connections between them.",
    category: "Updates",
    status: "draft",
    updated: "2026-11-06T09:00:00.000Z",
  },
  {
    id: "type",
    title: "Typography that does the quiet work",
    slug: "typography-that-works",
    summary: "Making reading and action feel like part of the same system.",
    body: "Type establishes a rhythm before anyone reads a word. Keep the relationships between headings, body text, and controls deliberate.",
    category: "Guides",
    status: "published",
    updated: "2026-11-05T14:00:00.000Z",
  },
  {
    id: "patterns",
    title: "Patterns worth keeping",
    slug: "patterns-worth-keeping",
    summary: "A working collection of decisions we would make again.",
    body: "A pattern earns its place when it helps someone make a useful decision with less effort.",
    category: "Stories",
    status: "draft",
    updated: "2026-11-04T08:00:00.000Z",
  },
  {
    id: "research",
    title: "Notes from the latest research",
    slug: "research-notes",
    summary: "What we learned by watching people use the product.",
    body: "Observe what people do before deciding what to change. The most useful improvements often address a small recurring friction.",
